sshpick 0.1.0

  ▌ sshpick [options] [command | query ...]

  For picker help, run `sshpick pick --help`

  Commands:

    pick       Pick a host and ssh to it (default)
    help       Show help for a command
    inspect    Show where a host resolves
    ls | list  List the hosts that match a query


  Global Options:

  -h,  --help             Output usage information
       --no-color         No color mode (default off)
       --non-interactive  Never open the picker; connect only when exactly one host matches
  -V,  --version          Output the version number


  Environment:

  NO_COLOR        No color; bold, dim and reverse video stay on a terminal
  CLICOLOR_FORCE  Keep color when output is not a terminal


  Exit Status:

  0    Success; after a pick, ssh's own status
  1    No host matches
  2    Usage, config or ssh -G error; several matches where one is needed
  127  ssh could not be run
  130  Cancelled


  Examples:

  - Open the picker with every host

    $ sshpick

  - Open it filtered to hosts matching both words

    $ sshpick new consul

  - Print the matching host names for a script

    $ sshpick ls new consul | cut -f2

  - Show where a host resolves

    $ sshpick inspect stg-consul1

  - Search for a word that is also a command name

    $ sshpick pick list

  Documentation:

    https://github.com/PunGrumpy/sshpick#readme
